course: dictionary
lesson: 3300
title: Ethane
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Ethane is a gas. You cannot see it or smell it, and it is made of carbon and hydrogen. A scientist would say it is a chemical, but the simple idea is this: it is a gas that burns easily. «Titan has rivers, lakes and seas, but they are filled with liquid methane and ethane, not water.» Here the words «not water» are the clue: the lakes are full of something else, and that something is ethane.
explain: The sentence puts methane and ethane together, so they must be alike. Both are gases here on Earth, and both belong to the same family of fuels. Look at the words around ethane: «liquid», «lakes» and «not water». Titan is so cold that ethane becomes a liquid there, even though on Earth it is a gas.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence instead of the hard word? You could put «methane» or «gas» in its place, and the sentence still makes sense. That tells you ethane is a substance, not a place or a thing you can hold like a rock.
fact: Ethane is a gas with no colour and no smell.
fact: Ethane is made of carbon and hydrogen. Its formula is C2H6: two carbon atoms and six hydrogen atoms.
fact: Ethane burns easily, and factories use it to make plastics.
fact: Ethane is found in natural gas, along with methane, propane and butane.
fact: On Titan, a moon of Saturn, the cold is so great that ethane is liquid and fills lakes and seas.
exercise: Which two gases are named together in the Titan sentence? | water and ice | *methane and ethane | carbon and hydrogen | oxygen and nitrogen
exercise: What is ethane, according to its meaning? | A solid used to make bread | *A gas with no colour or smell, made of carbon and hydrogen | A liquid that fills lakes, just like water | A metal used to build bridges
exercise: «Titan has rivers, lakes and seas, but they are filled with liquid methane and ethane, not water.» What do the words «not water» tell you? | The lakes are hot water | The lakes are frozen solid | *The lakes are filled with something other than water | The lakes are dry
test: Ethane is used in factories for what purpose? | *To make plastics | To grow crops | To make paper | To cool drinks
test: What does the formula C2H6 mean? | *Two carbon atoms and six hydrogen atoms | Six carbon atoms and two hydrogen atoms | One carbon atom and six hydrogen atoms | Two oxygen atoms and six carbon atoms
exam: Which of these gases has the formula C2H6? | butane | *ethane | propane | methane
